From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Darren Shepherd <darren@obot.ai>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 09:25:02 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] input: a link highlights on a plain hover, not only under
 ctrl

A URL in a Windows Terminal ghostty pane was not visibly a link until ctrl
was held, and neither was an OSC 8 hyperlink an application had marked.
Reported from use, against the cascadia pane in the same window, which
underlines a URL as soon as the pointer is on it and dotted-underlines
every OSC 8 cell whether the pointer is near it or not.

Three gates said ctrl, and they had to go together: the underline is drawn
from one of them and the reported link comes from another, so moving one
alone makes a pane that highlights text it will not report, or reports a
link it does not draw.

- `Config.default` registers the built-in URL link with
  `.highlight = .{ .hover_mods = ctrlOrSuper }`. Now `.hover`.
- `Surface.linkAtPos` looked at a cell's hyperlink data only when the mouse
  mods *equal* ctrl-or-super - so ctrl+shift found nothing either. Gone.
- The renderer's OSC 8 pass tested that same equality before asking for the
  highlighted cell set. Gone.

This is a deliberate divergence from upstream, not a bug fix. Upstream's
rule is defensible for a terminal that owns its own click; this fork's
embedder does not own it. Windows Terminal answers a ctrl+click itself, on
the press, from `GetHyperlink`, and never forwards it to the surface - so
nothing here makes a plain click open a link. The highlight is the preview
and only the preview.

One test, on the config default, because that is the value a rebase onto a
new upstream pin would silently revert.

zig build test: 3106 passed, 56 skipped, 0 failed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qm2sT9zLC2AndHGSanf2ws
---
 src/Surface.zig          | 10 ++++++++--
 src/config/Config.zig    | 29 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 src/renderer/generic.zig |  8 ++++----
 3 files changed, 39 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/Surface.zig b/src/Surface.zig
index 8f2f674d5..06f40b9b8 100644
--- a/src/Surface.zig
+++ b/src/Surface.zig
@@ -4410,8 +4410,14 @@ fn linkAtPos(
     // Get our comparison mods
     const mouse_mods = self.mouseModsWithCapture(self.mouse.mods);
 
-    // If we have the proper modifiers set then we can check for OSC8 links.
-    if (mouse_mods.equal(input.ctrlOrSuper(.{}))) hyperlink: {
+    // An OSC8 hyperlink is checked with no modifier requirement. Upstream
+    // asks for ctrl-or-super here, which hides an application's own links
+    // until a modifier is held; every other terminal - Windows Terminal's
+    // cascadia engine included - marks them as soon as the pointer is over
+    // them, and an application that emits OSC 8 has said outright that this
+    // text is a link. Opening one still takes a ctrl+click: the embedder owns
+    // the click, and the highlight is only the preview.
+    hyperlink: {
         const rac = mouse_pin.rowAndCell();
         const cell = rac.cell;
         if (!cell.hyperlink) break :hyperlink;
diff --git a/src/config/Config.zig b/src/config/Config.zig
index 55be18012..35f477fcc 100644
--- a/src/config/Config.zig
+++ b/src/config/Config.zig
@@ -3962,11 +3962,17 @@ pub fn default(alloc_gpa: Allocator) Allocator.Error!Config {
     // Add our default command palette entries
     try result.@"command-palette-entry".init(alloc);
 
-    // Add our default link for URL detection
+    // Add our default link for URL detection.
+    //
+    // `.hover` rather than upstream's `.{ .hover_mods = ctrlOrSuper }`: a URL
+    // underlines as soon as the pointer is over it, which is what Windows
+    // Terminal's cascadia engine does and what this fork's panes are compared
+    // against. The modifier still gates *opening* it - that is the embedder's
+    // ctrl+click - so this only changes the preview.
     try result.link.links.append(alloc, .{
         .regex = url.regex,
         .action = .{ .open = {} },
-        .highlight = .{ .hover_mods = inputpkg.ctrlOrSuper(.{}) },
+        .highlight = .{ .hover = {} },
     });
 
     return result;
@@ -4016,6 +4022,25 @@ pub fn loadEntry(
     try self.loadIter(alloc, &iter);
 }
 
+test "the default URL link highlights on a plain hover" {
+    const testing = std.testing;
+    const alloc = testing.allocator;
+
+    var cfg: Config = try .default(alloc);
+    defer cfg.deinit();
+
+    // Upstream's default here is `.{ .hover_mods = ctrlOrSuper }`, which shows
+    // nothing until ctrl is held. A ghostty pane is judged beside a cascadia
+    // pane in the same Windows Terminal window, and that one underlines a URL
+    // on a plain hover - so a rebase that quietly restores the modifier is a
+    // regression, and this is what catches it. Opening the link still takes a
+    // ctrl+click; the embedder owns the click.
+    try testing.expectEqual(@as(usize, 1), cfg.link.links.items.len);
+    try testing.expect(
+        std.meta.activeTag(cfg.link.links.items[0].highlight) == .hover,
+    );
+}
+
 test "loadEntry sets a value" {
     const testing = std.testing;
     const alloc = testing.allocator;
diff --git a/src/renderer/generic.zig b/src/renderer/generic.zig
index 69b0e5cc8..4a7f2dc1c 100644
--- a/src/renderer/generic.zig
+++ b/src/renderer/generic.zig
@@ -5,7 +5,6 @@ const wuffs = @import("wuffs");
 const apprt = @import("../apprt.zig");
 const configpkg = @import("../config.zig");
 const font = @import("../font/main.zig");
-const inputpkg = @import("../input.zig");
 const os = @import("../os/main.zig");
 const terminal = @import("../terminal/main.zig");
 const renderer = @import("../renderer.zig");
@@ -1262,9 +1261,10 @@ pub fn Renderer(comptime GraphicsAPI: type) type {
                     // If our mouse isn't hovering, we have no links.
                     const vp = state.mouse.point orelse break :osc8 .empty;
 
-                    // If the right mods aren't pressed, then we can't match.
-                    if (!state.mouse.mods.equal(inputpkg.ctrlOrSuper(.{})))
-                        break :osc8 .empty;
+                    // No modifier requirement: Surface.linkAtPos highlights
+                    // an OSC8 link on a plain hover, and the two have to agree
+                    // about which cells are lit or the underline appears
+                    // without the link being reported (or the reverse).
 
                     break :osc8 self.terminal_state.linkCells(
                         arena_alloc,
